":{"commit_sha":"ab1d457d8759229d615e70a8f37ed8c7395815be","position":"1787152886204837001-8effe69d-c93b-48b7-b80a-f3bed6e5e419"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ca74ce2f5d8952c86221f83f8dcb8cd3eef7d4acec8a241b17a6d8e6a9e633a2","event_uuid":"142452d1-4ec6-4c55-aa44-0633a21a1b35","position":{"commit_sha":"c494e7d3bdcf47c9711300d90902331996edd91b","position":"1787153490416054001-142452d1-4ec6-4c55-aa44-0633a21a1b35"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"424929610dc3f2235c8a4296162fb6f2de2ac192c9c8c85e78e0d88720d932b9","event_uuid":"54a575b0-6249-4f20-a151-9126b96e9eac","position":{"commit_sha":"1af4e9fa9fd44492f6f65041b3f66a50a3479831","position":"1787153662412592001-54a575b0-6249-4f20-a151-9126b96e9eac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d1c6d55f4df98211ee4c630dcf947ad446dd426098690a44c7f7138443732831","event_uuid":"71212471-2b60-45f9-931b-ef25c9b9faed","position":{"commit_sha":"1af4e9fa9fd44492f6f65041b3f66a50a3479831","position":"1787153663312546001-71212471-2b60-45f9-931b-ef25c9b9faed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787081615601659001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"03ef6987-b664-479e-8673-f52ea09ff390","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8"},{"link_uuid":"f3c0a7dc-8c11-48f7-9868-f11fc8d2df81","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"},{"link_uuid":"eaf78e9d-d0dd-40e2-8bda-1187808b2091","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4f6b-88ea-e3ff-4661"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOperators need an authoritative configuration precedence/source/lifecycle reference and a security reference that stay byte-current with the config schema and the deprecation/secret-name registries rather than drifting by hand. The existing `docs/config.md` is a 648-line HAND-AUTHORED operator doc (rationale, precedence narrative, a `## Config-key inventory`, a `### Secrets` list, the `## ticket.default_assignee` section, a fail-loud tombstone-registry section, stable anchor slugs) with many in-repo consumers: content-asserting tests (`test_snapshot_docs.py`, `test_session_id.py`, `test_structured_run.py`, `test_harness_provenance.py`, `test_session_shims.py`, `test_agents_claim_assignee_guidance.py`, `test_build_drift.py`, `test_llm_model_env_removal.py`), anchor deep links (`AGENTS.md#ticketdefault_assignee`, `docs/reuse-surface.md#rebar_operation_snapshot_shadow`, `docs/concurrency.md#config-key-inventory`),. Byte-generating into `config.md` would strand these consumers.\n\n## Outcome\nA new `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` generates a NEW standalone, fully-generated `docs/config-reference.md` (the machine-current, registry-derived precedence/source/lifecycle reference) and a NEW indexed `docs/security.md`. Its concrete inputs are three symbols: the typed config schema `rebar._config_schema` (keys/types/defaults), `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY` + `rebar._deprecations.tombstones()` filtered to `kind==\"cfg\"` (the per-key LIFECYCLE/deprecation/removal column — a NEW cfg-channel derivation modelled on how `gen_env_registry.py` reads `kind==\"env\"` entries), and `rebar._child_env._ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES` (the secret-name inventory). There is no discrete \"ownership registry\" (ownership is a DERIVED AST classification in `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`); the generator does NOT read it. `docs/config.md` is LEFT ENTIRELY UNCHANGED, so all its consumers stay intact by construction. Non-registry-derivable narrative topics named by the epic (precedence rule, observability exception, subprocess limitations, behavior deltas, native refresh) are supplied VERBATIM from a curated template constant in the generator, not synthesized. `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation reference the new docs. A newline-normalizing `--check` drift mode, gated by a pytest suite (run under `make test`, no CI dependency), fails when either generated doc is stale.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` (modelled on `gen_env_registry.py`/`gen_cli_reference.py`): read `rebar._config_schema` (keys/types/defaults), `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY` + `rebar._deprecations.tombstones()` (`kind==\"cfg\"` → lifecycle column), and `rebar._child_env._ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES` (secret-name inventory), and render (a) registry-derived tables and (b) the curated template constant (the precedence/observability/subprocess/behavior-delta/native-refresh narrative, verbatim) into fully-generated `docs/config-reference.md` and `docs/security.md`. Both are generated whole (no partial-region markers — new generator-owned files). Each carries a top-of-file markdown banner within its first 8 lines containing the word \"generated\" AND the exact command `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py`, per `test_generated_surface_markers.py::test_text_surface_carries_a_banner`. The generator exposes `main([\"--check\"])` returning 0 when the committed docs match and nonzero on drift (as `gen_cli_reference.py`/`gen_env_registry.py` do).\n2. Create `docs/config-reference.md` and `docs/security.md`; update `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation. Register BOTH docs in the parity gate: add each (→ `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py`) to the `GENERATED` map in `tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py`, AND add a matching row for each to the `### Generated — never edit these by hand` TABLE in `docs/README.md` — the table row set must EQUAL `GENERATED`+`GATED_HAND_AUTHORED` (`test_readme_table_matches_registry`), so the prose nav link is not sufficient. Do NOT modify `docs/config.md`.\n3. Add pytest suite `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` (modelled on `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`) that asserts `gen.main([\"--check\"]) == 0` on the committed docs and drives the topic/preservation/newline coverage below. This is the DRIFT GATE and it runs under `make test` — portable, no CI provider required; `--check` compares with newline normalization (universal-newline / text-mode read, not raw byte compare) so a CRLF autocrlf checkout does not false-fail.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Drift: a deliberate edit to either generated file makes `gen.main([\"--check\"])` return nonzero; regenerating clears it.\n- Preservation (by construction): `docs/config.md` is byte-unchanged, proven by a test asserting the generator/`--check` never target `config.md`; its content-asserting suites named in Context continue to pass.\n- Topic coverage: a test asserts that, across `docs/config-reference.md` and `docs/security.md` together, a heading/anchor exists for every entry in an explicit REQUIRED_TOPICS list — precedence, source, lifecycle, restart/redeploy rotation, native refresh, observability exception, subprocess limitations, behavior deltas, MCP/CLI exposure — failing if any is missing.\n- Newline safety: a regression test feeds CRLF-encoded checked-out content while the generator emits LF and asserts `--check` reports NO drift.\n- Parity gate: `tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py` passes — each new doc carries its self-announcing banner (`test_text_surface_carries_a_banner`) and the `docs/README.md` table row set equals the registry (`test_readme_table_matches_registry`).\n- Portability: the generator and its `--check` drift gate run under `make test` with no CI provider present.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDocs-and-tooling only; no product-behavior change. `docs/config.md` and all its consumers are untouched. Rollback removes the generator (with its `--check` mode), the curated template constant, `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/security.md`, `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py`, the two `GENERATED`-map/README-table registrations, and reverts the two navigation edits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` generates `docs/config-reference.md` and `docs/security.md` whole from `rebar._config_schema`, `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY`+`tombstones()` (cfg lifecycle), and `rebar._child_env._ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES`, plus a curated template constant, and never writes `docs/config.md`.\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` is byte-unchanged and all its enumerated consumers remain intact (its content-asserting suites pass; its anchor slugs still resolve), proven by a test that the generator/`--check` do not target `config.md`.\n- [ ] Across `docs/config-reference.md` and `docs/security.md`, an anchor exists for every topic in the REQUIRED_TOPICS list (precedence, source, lifecycle, restart/redeploy rotation, native refresh, observability exception, subprocess limitations, behavior deltas, MCP/CLI exposure), proven by a topic-coverage test.\n- [ ] `docs/config-reference.md` carries a top-of-file banner (within its first 8 lines) naming `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py`, and `docs/security.md` carries the same, satisfying `test_generated_surface_markers.py::test_text_surface_carries_a_banner`.\n- [ ] Both new docs are registered in the `GENERATED` map of `tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py` and in the `docs/README.md` `### Generated — never edit these by hand` table, so `test_readme_table_matches_registry` passes.\n- [ ] `gen.main([\"--check\"])` returns 0 on committed docs and nonzero on a stale doc, is exercised by `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` under `make test` with no CI dependency, and does NOT false-fail on a CRLF checkout (newline-normalized comparison).\n- [ ] `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation reference the new docs.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"new generator: registry-derived tables + curated template into config-reference.md + security.md"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"new fully-generated config reference"},{"path":"docs/security.md","reason":"new indexed security reference"},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"navigation update"},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"navigation update"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"wire drift check into make lint"},{"path":"scripts/check_config_reference_drift.py","reason":"newline-normalized drift check"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_config_reference_drift.py","reason":"held-out oracle: drift, preservation, topic-coverage, CRLF safety"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"],["depends_on","29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8"],["parent","aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4"],["relates_to","4f6b-88ea-e3ff-4661"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4","parent_status_uuid":"54a575b0-6249-4f20-a151-9126b96e9eac","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3199-d739-8804-4746","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.4 — Generate config/security/operator docs from registries + drift check","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1e3f59b5-123d-449d-aefb-4d5f3a1ca01f","5ef73a67-b1f8-43cc-9871-414621e12fd6","15ca5e2d-b334-4102-a60d-ada9e50edbad","a8c6368e-3aa9-48f4-97fe-dcc25b859a71","5d01bfd6-9a6c-489f-b753-9a8e7a08c62e","ee376bb3-df4d-4dc8-a103-3d22043c3848","d4f020c4-445c-4083-808c-255ff7bffbb9","7826b217-ac5e-4111-b803-933277e8562b","eaf78e9d-d0dd-40e2-8bda-1187808b2091","8effe69d-c93b-48b7-b80a-f3bed6e5e419","142452d1-4ec6-4c55-aa44-0633a21a1b35","54a575b0-6249-4f20-a151-9126b96e9eac","71212471-2b60-45f9-931b-ef25c9b9faed"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787153663312546002,"uuid":"cc79f04d-b3d2-4791-a8c1-63f8c3bc0095"}